NOTES:- `AuthProvider` is not mounted anywhere yet (root layout wasn't in scope). Until it wraps the app (e.g. in `app/layout.tsx`), `useAuthUser()` returns the context default `{ user: null, loading: true }`, so `KindredHeader` will render the signed-out "in" link.
- Per spec, `components/kindred-shell.tsx` is now a client module. Any SERVER component that imports the plain-data export `seededCampaigns` from it will receive a client-reference stub rather than the array (client-module exports become references across the RSC boundary). Flagged since a later task removes these exports anyway; if a server page breaks on `.map`, that page needs to become a client component or the data must move.
- Login assumes Supabase email auto-confirm is enabled. If "Confirm email" is on, `signUp` succeeds without creating a session; the redirect then lands the user signed-out and they must confirm via email and sign in.
- Middleware degrades gracefully (skips refresh/protection) if the `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_*` vars are missing, keeping public pages alive; `lib/supabase/*` helpers throw loudly instead, matching `lib/server/supabase-admin.ts` style.
- Sign-out responds 303 so browsers convert the POST into a GET navigation to `/`.
- `authedFetch` merges caller headers via `new Headers(init?.headers)` and always wins for `Authorization`/`content-type`; it tolerates empty/non-JSON bodies (treated as `null`).
